---
/**
 * Feature 3 - Getting Raindrop's conversations into Kitaru.
 *
 * There is no built-in importer, so the graphic leads with that rather than
 * hiding it, then shows the two routes and what each one buys. The accent
 * marks the path that gets full replay.
 */
---

<figure class="fig">
  <div class="banner">
    <span class="banner-key">No built-in Raindrop importer</span>
    <span class="banner-val">Importers cover Langfuse, LangSmith, Braintrust, Logfire, and Arize Phoenix</span>
  </div>

  <div class="paths">
    <div class="path path--accent">
      <div class="path-head">
        <span class="path-tag path-tag--accent">Path 1</span>
        <span class="path-name">Record beside it</span>
      </div>
      <div class="flow">
        <span class="node">your agent</span>
        <span class="flow-arrow" aria-hidden="true">&rarr;</span>
        <span class="node node--accent mono">kitaru adapter</span>
        <span class="flow-arrow" aria-hidden="true">&rarr;</span>
        <span class="node node--accent">session</span>
      </div>
      <div class="path-note">
        Keep sending events to Raindrop. Adapters exist for PydanticAI,
        LangGraph, OpenAI Agents SDK, Mastra, and Vercel AI SDK.
      </div>
      <div class="gets gets--accent">
        <span class="gets-key">Buys you</span>
        <span class="gets-val">full replay: overrides and tool policies, because the adapter is in the process</span>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="path">
      <div class="path-head">
        <span class="path-tag">Path 2</span>
        <span class="path-name">Import an export</span>
      </div>
      <div class="flow">
        <span class="node">CSV or Query API</span>
        <span class="flow-arrow" aria-hidden="true">&rarr;</span>
        <span class="node mono">parse()</span>
        <span class="flow-arrow" aria-hidden="true">&rarr;</span>
        <span class="node">session</span>
      </div>
      <div class="path-note">
        A custom importer is one function that yields sessions from a file.
        Enterprise adds warehouse exports.
      </div>
      <div class="gets">
        <span class="gets-key">Buys you</span>
        <span class="gets-val">investigate, evaluate, and cohort. Replay still needs the agent's run command</span>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="carry">
    <span class="carry-arrow" aria-hidden="true">&darr;</span>
    <span class="carry-text">
      Either way, a Raindrop issue points at events. You freeze the same
      conversations, recorded as sessions, into a cohort.
    </span>
  </div>
</figure>

<style>
  .fig {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 12px;
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
  }

  .banner {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 3px;
    padding: 10px 12px;
    border: 1px dashed var(--color-border);
    border-radius: 10px;
    background: var(--color-surface-warm);
  }
  .banner-key {
    font-size: 9.5px;
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--color-muted);
  }
  .banner-val { font-size: 11px; line-height: 1.4; color: var(--color-secondary); }

  .paths {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
    gap: 12px;
  }
  .path {
    border: 1px solid var(--color-border);
    border-radius: 12px;
    padding: 14px;
    background: var(--color-surface);
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 10px;
  }
  .path--accent { border-color: var(--color-accent); }

  .path-head { display: flex; align-items: baseline; gap: 8px; }
  .path-tag {
    font-size: 9px;
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--color-muted);
  }
  .path-tag--accent { color: var(--color-accent); }
  .path-name { font-size: 12px; font-weight: 700; color: var(--color-primary); }

  .flow {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 5px;
  }
  .node {
    padding: 4px 8px;
    border: 1px solid var(--color-border-light);
    border-radius: 6px;
    background: var(--color-bg);
    font-size: 10px;
    color: var(--color-secondary);
  }
  .node--accent {
    border-color: var(--color-accent);
    background: var(--color-accent-light);
    color: var(--color-accent-deep);
    font-weight: 700;
  }
  .flow-arrow { font-size: 12px; color: var(--color-muted); }
  .mono { font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 9.5px; }

  .path-note {
    font-size: 10.5px;
    line-height: 1.5;
    color: var(--color-muted);
  }

  .gets {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 3px;
    margin-top: auto;
    padding: 8px 10px;
    border-radius: 8px;
    background: var(--color-surface-subtle);
    border: 1px solid var(--color-border-light);
  }
  .gets--accent { background: var(--color-accent-light); border-color: var(--color-border-accent); }
  .gets-key {
    font-size: 9px;
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--color-muted);
  }
  .gets--accent .gets-key { color: var(--color-accent); }
  .gets-val { font-size: 10.5px; line-height: 1.4; color: var(--color-primary); }

  .carry {
    display: flex;
    align-items: flex-start;
    gap: 9px;
    padding-top: 10px;
    border-top: 1px dashed var(--color-border-light);
  }
  .carry-arrow { font-size: 13px; color: var(--color-accent); line-height: 1.3; }
  .carry-text { font-size: 10.5px; line-height: 1.5; color: var(--color-secondary); }

  @media (max-width: 720px) {
    .paths { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
    .gets { margin-top: 0; }
  }
</style>
